{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T09:34:06.814770Z","id":"e2e8e49f15594dcbef17d608e5ca19ebf6ccb913a5e4f48f65f4c2b7a0d4749f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs:1413-1420 refuses any reader_view (docs/contract.md:10438 says the same, and the fixture's own script step at :980-995 shows it refused), yet the example a host copies first carries one. The wire round-trip test (crates/clax-surface/src/tests/wire/mod.rs) passes because the type accepts the member. The native daemon sets content from Store::keeps_bot_content (crates/clax-http/src/state.rs:477), true for the fs store, and the fixture's script shows nothing withheld. Other places where the examples disagree: the MessageResponse for seq 2 says waiting: true while the events deliver messages [1, 2] at step 3 before `parked` at step 4; run-2 ends gave_up as e2 in one ServeResponse and stopped/cancelled as e5 and in its RunState; docs/contract.md:10816-10863 shows seq 2 waiting: false and messages: [2].","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"580ed779703b255826670ea2184045c7677a7286ecf41380dde04f0547b86de9"},"suggested_fix":"Drop reader_view from the first RegisterRequest, show an empty withheld (or say which store withholds snapshot), and make the message/event examples tell one run's story.","summary":"The fixture's first RegisterRequest gives `reader_view: \"none\"`, which the daemon refuses `invalid_settings`, and its Registered answer (:55-66) and docs/contract.md:10401-10402 show `snapshot` withheld for `content`, which no daemon serving these routes withholds","tags":["review","docs","fixture","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T10:27:18.655228Z","id":"2ecc132333dda8976f807195680e8ad0375084a6177cbb5abb1746ea5fe9942e","body":{"detail":"The manifest RegisterRequest gives no reader_view; the Registered with a withheld snapshot is removed and docs/contract.md's Registering example shows none; MessageResponse seq 2 is waiting: false, a third message (seq 3) is waiting: true, matching events that give [1, 2] at step 3 and park at step 4 and the parked RunState's messages_waiting 1; the stopped/cancelled RunState and end e5 are run-3's, as e3 is. docs/contract.md's messages example gives [1, 2] and a third while parked. clax_surface_lib_test (every_message_of_the_fixture_is_written_as_it_is_read) passes. Proposed close for the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"e2e8e49f15594dcbef17d608e5ca19ebf6ccb913a5e4f48f65f4c2b7a0d4749f","summary":"Fixed in 445b54810: the fixture and the contract tell one daemon's story","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T15:06:55.115953Z","id":"a48c94c4f64de07e7cf105d84d64497336d953d2673a809bc7933dd46cb1e563","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8407e7367","summary":"Fixed by 8407e7367 (first committed as 445b54810, re-created signed): tests::wire::every_message_of_the_fixture_is_written_as_it_is_read over docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json passes on claxbot-surfaces at cd563c6f5 (bazelisk test //crates/clax-surface:clax_surface_lib_test)","supersedes":"e2e8e49f15594dcbef17d608e5ca19ebf6ccb913a5e4f48f65f4c2b7a0d4749f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:51:01.323719Z","id":"5369417fe65b50cae08937f04f0a3e0ac9c202b2839ac7e98f953e55907e7f72","body":{"detail":"The hub test that replays the script enqueues every `run: call` with `retry: Retry::NONE` (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs:240-260, and `call` at :68-77), while a run on the daemon has `Retry::DAEMON`, three attempts one second apart and then two (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs:633-642; docs/contract.md:10621-10624). Two steps therefore show what the daemon does not do: at at_ms 59 the host answers `$lamps4` with `unavailable` and the script is thrown it in the same instant (on the daemon it is sent again after 1 s and 2 s first, docs/contract.md:10573-10576); at at_ms 40000 a read of an unconnected but held registration is thrown `unavailable` at once (on the daemon it waits for its host until its deadline, docs/contract.md:10641-10648). docs/contract.md:10287-10288 and 10976-10989 present the script as the daemon's story that a host's own tests can replay; a host author who reads those steps as the daemon's behaviour builds a host that expects fast failure and no resend.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"460f0e206fdf461435349a81d3bde4b4c2ca47438e6a129cc6e495c5e7c1c30d"},"suggested_fix":"Either state in the fixture's `about` and in docs/contract.md \"The fixture\" that the script's calls are made under a policy that sends nothing again (one attempt; the daemon's runs have three), and give each `run: call` step a `policy` member the replay reads; or add a `policy` member, default the daemon's, re-script the at_ms 59 and at_ms 40000 steps under it, and add one step of a call sent again after `unavailable`.","summary":"The fixture's script is the life of calls under a policy that sends nothing again, not the daemon's, and says so nowhere","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:51:01.323779Z","id":"3eab9a55004cf0ed0c5222bd35ff51eeb68443a520a519554083fb0131e84f4a","body":{"detail":"The fixture's surface declares `tidy(request: { ask: Instruction }): { summary: string }` (contract.json `files[\"desk.d.ts\"]`; the manifest's `tidy` has no message type), and docs/contract.md:10830-10832 says a kind with one parameter takes no messages (400 `takes_no_messages`, crates/clax-surface/src/wire.rs:90-92). Yet `messages` holds three `MessageRequest`s answered `seq` 1-3 (contract.json:374-420), a `step` event of run-1 with `messages: [1, 2]` (:331-345), and `RunState`s of run-1 and run-3 of kind `tidy` with `messages_waiting` 1 and 2 and `undelivered: [2, 3]` (:427-470). The contract's own example of messages uses a surface `inbox` that the fixture does not define (docs/contract.md:10835). Likewise the `ServeResponse` example has call `c4` with no `expires_in_ms` and args `[\"No deadline.\"]` (contract.json:215-224), though docs/contract.md:10558-10559 says every call the daemon sends has a deadline. docs/contract.md:10287-10288 promises examples that \"tell one coherent story\" a host's tests can replay; a host test that registers `desk` and sends these messages is refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"7c54c272d003efb635b24cfe1a62a08f1d93542717b1e465cb5ed9362c894838"},"suggested_fix":"Give the fixture's surface a kind that takes messages (for example `tidy(request: { ask: Instruction }, message?: { say: Instruction }): { summary: string }` in both notations, with the hash updated) or add a second kind for it and put the message examples on a run of that kind; use the same surface in the contract's example at docs/contract.md:10835; give `c4` an `expires_in_ms`, or move a call without one to `tolerated` with why.","summary":"The fixture's message, event and run-state examples are of run-1 of kind `tidy`, which takes no messages, so no daemon would produce or accept them together","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:55:56.850567Z","id":"171d636006194ed90adf93fb7b8d58f223dd3795df688ae4954ab7a9ec825369","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs:251-260 enqueues each script `call` with `retry: Retry::NONE` (also `call` at :68-77). Script steps: at_ms 59 the host answers `$lamps4` `unavailable` and the next step at the same at_ms is the script's `outcome` `unavailable`; at_ms 40000 a call of `$a` (unconnected, still held) is `error: unavailable` at once. Under `Delivery::DAEMON`/`Retry::DAEMON` (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs:633-642) the first is sent again and the second waits (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs:3369; docs/contract.md:10641-10648). The fixture's `about` and docs/contract.md:10965-10995 name no policy.","kind":"comment","references":"5369417fe65b50cae08937f04f0a3e0ac9c202b2839ac7e98f953e55907e7f72","summary":"confirmed: the script replays under `Retry::NONE`, and neither the fixture nor the contract says so","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/claxbot-surfaces/contract.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:55:56.851029Z","id":"68a4f260536d759d7d3e748a28810eb61ccdfba7dcd02b2529fd23a1b1807e91","body":{"detail":"contract.json `files[\"desk.d.ts\"]` declares `tidy(request: { ask: Instruction }): { summary: string }` (one parameter). docs/contract.md:10830-10832: a kind with one parameter takes no messages; crates/clax-surface/src/wire.rs:90-92 `CODE_TAKES_NO_MESSAGES`. Yet `messages` holds three `MessageRequest`s answered seq 1-3, a `step` event of run-1 with `messages: [1, 2]`, and `RunState`s of kind `tidy` with `messages_waiting` 1 and 2 and `undelivered: [2, 3]`. The `ServeResponse` call `c4` (notify, args `[\"No deadline.\"]`) has no `expires_in_ms`, against docs/contract.md:10558-10559 \"Every call has a deadline\".","kind":"comment","references":"3eab9a55004cf0ed0c5222bd35ff51eeb68443a520a519554083fb0131e84f4a","summary":"confirmed: message, event and run-state examples are of `tidy`, which takes no messages; `c4` has no deadline","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
